    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph_number": 288,
      "text": "Internal units are patients; external records are hospitalization episodes. External patients may contribute multiple episodes. The early and late comparisons share the same one-year non-event controls; their displayed sizes must not be added to reconstruct the primary cohort.",
      "display_html": "Internal units are patients; external records are hospitalization episodes. External patients may contribute multiple episodes. The early and late comparisons share the same one-year non-event controls; their displayed sizes must not be added to reconstruct the primary cohort."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "paragraph_number": 289,
      "text": "Two external event episodes with unclassifiable timing remain in the one-year analysis and are excluded from both time groups. The repeated count in the two external rows denotes the same two episodes.",
      "display_html": "Two external event episodes with unclassifiable timing remain in the one-year analysis and are excluded from both time groups. The repeated count in the two external rows denotes the same two episodes."
    },
